  {
    "pkattachmentId": 38918,
    "bookid": 36,
    "chapterId": 277,
    "fileId": 20862,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Key differential diagnoses of diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL)</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Kikkeri N. Naresh",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; border: none; \" border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\" \">\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Entity</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.3pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; \">Morphology</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 244.3pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"326\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; \">Key additional features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>EBV+ DLBCL</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.3pt; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Monomorphic and polymorphic types identified; usually has large areas of necrosis; cells resembling Hodgkin/Reed&ndash;Sternberg cells can be seen</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 244.3pt; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"326\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">EBV+ (as demonstrated by EBER in&nbsp;situ hybridization) is seen in most lymphoma cells <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{29984868}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; border: none; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; \">Monomorphic posttransplant lymphoproliferative disorder of DLBCL type</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.3pt; border: none; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; \">Similar to DLBCL</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 244.3pt; border: none; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"326\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; \">Can be EBV+; transplanted kidney can be a site for the development of DLBCL </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{18318740}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>High-grade B-cell lymphoma with <em style=\"\">MYC</em>, <em style=\"\">BCL2</em>, and/or <em style=\"\">BCL6</em> rearrangement</strong> <span class=\"Ref-PMID\"><span style=\"\">{27447126}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.3pt; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Can be similar to DLBCL, with some features overlapping with those of Burkitt lymphoma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 244.3pt; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"326\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">FISH analysis for <em style=\"\">MYC</em>, <em style=\"\">BCL6</em>, and <em style=\"\">BCL2</em> rearrangements is essential for the confirmation of this diagnosis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; border: none; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; \">Intravascular large B-cell lymphoma</span></strong> <span class=\"Ref-PMID\"><span style=\"\">{28381751; 32367674}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.3pt; border: none; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; \">Presence of clusters of large CD20+ B&nbsp;cells within small vessels; about one&nbsp;third of cases express PDL1</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 244.3pt; border: none; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"326\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; \">Can be rarely encountered in a renal biopsy</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Seminoma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.3pt; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Monomorphic large cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 244.3pt; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"326\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">KIT (CD117), podoplanin (D2-40), and OCT3/4 positivity is helpful in the distinction</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" \">\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; \">Spermatocytic tumour</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.3pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; \">Usually has a tripartite population of neoplastic cells, but an intermediate cell&ndash;predominant spermatocytic tumour may mimic DLBCL</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 244.3pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"326\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; \">Positivity for KIT (CD117) and negativity for B-cell markers help in the distinction</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; \">EBER, </span>EBV-encoded small RNA.</p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 38919,
    "bookid": 36,
    "chapterId": 277,
    "fileId": 20865,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Immunohistochemistry of diffuse large B-cell lymphoma</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Kikkeri N. Naresh",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.7pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Aspect</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 403.95pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"539\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Markers</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.7pt; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Defining feature</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 403.95pt; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"539\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Expression of one or more B-cell antigens (CD19, CD20, CD79a, PAX5)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.7pt; border: none; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Frequently positive</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 403.95pt; border: none; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"539\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CD45, BCL2, CD10, BCL6, IRF4 (MUM1)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.7pt; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Rarely positive</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 403.95pt; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"539\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CD5 expression in a subset of cases <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{18556402}</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Focal expression of cyclin&nbsp;D1 (in the absence of SOX11 expression) <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{22642745}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 134.7pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"180\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Always negative</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 403.95pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"539\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">T-cell antigens, TdT, and EBER</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">EBER, EBV-encoded small RNA.</p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 38920,
    "bookid": 36,
    "chapterId": 277,
    "fileId": 20867,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Key prognostic predictors (biomarkers) in diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL)</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Kikkeri N. Naresh",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; border: none; \" border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Biomarker</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 513.6pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"685\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Significance</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Hans classifier</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 513.6pt; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"685\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Subtyping into germinal-centre B-cell and non&ndash;germinal-centre categories based on the expression of CD10, BCL6, and IRF4 (MUM1) <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{14504078}</span>; the non&ndash;germinal-centre type has a poor prognosis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; border: none; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>MYC</em>-IG rearrangement</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 513.6pt; border: none; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"685\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">DLBCL with <em>MYC</em>-IG rearrangement is associated with a poor prognosis <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{26373676}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>MYC expression</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 513.6pt; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"685\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">MYC expression in &gt;&nbsp;70% of lymphoma cells is a strong indicator of a poor prognosis <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{32054654; 29954940}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.3pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"246\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>MYC and BCL2 dual expression</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 513.6pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"685\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Dual expressers are associated with a poor prognosis <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{22851565}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
    "imageUrl": null,
